    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file.\n\n### The Problem\nThe issue was in the `gate` command handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`. When Commander.js parsed the arguments for `frai gate init --ci`, it was consuming the global `--ci` option at the program level before it could be passed through to the `frai-gate` CLI. This meant the `args` array passed to the action handler only contained `['init']` without the `--ci` flag.\n\n### The Solution\nI modified the action handler to capture all arguments directly from `process.argv` instead of relying solely on Commander's parsed `args` parameter:\n\n```typescript\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst gateArgs = gateIndex >= 0 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : args ?? [];\n```\n\nThis bypasses Commander's option parsing and passes all arguments exactly as they appear on the command line to the `frai-gate` CLI, ensuring flags like `--ci` are properly forwarded.\n\n### Verification\n\u2705 Rebuilt the CLI with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\u2705 Tested the command: `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both:\n  - `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n  - `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`",
